WHAT IS OPEN SOURCE

The 100 developer tools listed in `opensource/manifest.json`, as published at
https://github.com/redbison-dev/redbison-tools, are MIT licensed. Their terms
are in `opensource/site/LICENSE` and they may be used, modified and self-hosted
freely under those terms. Nothing here narrows that grant.

WHAT IS NOT

Everything else, including:

  - the written guides, tool write-ups, worked examples and FAQ answers, and
    the research behind them;
  - the remaining tools, calculators and converters, and their logic;
  - the site's code, build pipeline and generated artefacts;
  - the RedBison name, logo and visual design.

That the site shows its formulas and cites its sources does not place them in
the public domain. Those are published so readers can check the answers, not
so the work can be reproduced elsewhere.

Reading the site, linking to it, quoting a short passage with attribution and
using the tools for your own work are all fine, and are covered by the terms at
https://redbison.dev/tos.

Enquiries, licensing requests and copyright reports: team@redbison.dev
